{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$x^4\\ln(x)$ is the product of two, more basic, expressions: $x^4$ and $\\ln(x)$.\n\nTherefore, $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ can be found using **the product rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)v(x)]\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)+u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=u'(x)v(x)+u(x)v'(x)\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^4\\ln(x))\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^4)\\ln(x)+x^4\\dfrac{d}{dx}(\\ln(x))\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{The product rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=4x^3\\cdot \\ln(x)+x^4\\cdot \\dfrac1x\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }x^4\\text{ and }\\ln(x)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=4x^3\\ln(x)+x^3\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Simplify}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=x^3(4\\ln(x)+1)\u0026\u0026\\gray{\\text{Factor out }x^3}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=x^3(4\\ln(x)+1)$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $y=x^4\\ln(x)$.\n\n**Find $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$x^3(4\\ln(x)+1)$","correct":true},{"content":"$4x^3(x^4+\\ln(x))$","correct":false},{"content":"$4x^3+\\dfrac1x$","isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$4x^2$","isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
